{"id":"twitter:1658912205243310080","tweet_id":"1658912205243310080","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1658912205243310080","title":"@KittenShovel @Myth_01010 @buttwhy_0_o @ukraine_map They were not bombing their own. Just stop Any analysis of how artillery was used during Putin's f","summary":"@KittenShovel @Myth_01010 @buttwhy_0_o @ukraine_map They were not bombing their own. Just stop Any analysis of how artillery was used during Putin's first phase of the war showed artillery as overwatch. This means it was like 5-8 km behind the infantry and would provide cover. Most of the shells fired were fro \"separatists\" https://t.co/D5QqOwWJRt","date":"2023-05-17","published":"2023-05-17T19:07:45+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/KittenShovel/status/1658900591215616007","reply_tweet_id":"1658900591215616007","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@KittenShovel @Myth_01010 @buttwhy_0_o @ukraine_map They were not bombing their own.<br><br> Just stop<br><br>Any analysis of how artillery was used during Putin&#x27;s first phase of the war showed artillery as overwatch.<br><br>This means it was like 5-8 km behind the infantry and would provide cover.<br><br>Most of the shells fired were fro &quot;separatists&quot; <a href=\"https://t.co/D5QqOwWJRt\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/D5QqOwWJRt</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/176f9b15416c02c5d5ef4cc74edc6044.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1658912205243310080","display_date":"May 17, 2023 · 19:07 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/176f9b15416c02c5d5ef4cc74edc6044.jpg"]}
